# covers: 0b E1.3, 0b E1.4, 0b E6.2, 1a E2.3
# 0b-reconnect: the socket is lost (nf.DropSocket, as a network failure); the client fetches a
# FRESH play ticket (tickets are single use), reconnects, and rebuilds its projections from the
# spawn stream: a second own EntitySpawn, the same entity id.
#
# Timeouts (R1): backoff 0.5 s + IssuePlayTicket (5 s deadline) + upgrade; 3x of 5.5 s rounded up.
nf.Login
nf.WaitFor connected 15
nf.EnterWorld
nf.WaitFor in_world 15
nf.Expect own_spawns == 1
nf.DropSocket
nf.WaitFor own_spawns >= 2 20     # the new session's spawn stream arrived
nf.WaitFor in_world 5
nf.Expect ticket_refreshed        # >= 2 tickets presented, the newest differs from the first
nf.Expect own_entity_unchanged
nf.Expect connected
nf.Within 60
